/**
 * FY2027 House General Appropriations Bill (HGAB) importer.
 *
 * Reads the payloads generated by the BetterGov DPWH-NEP-HB-2027-ANALYSIS
 * workbench (a checkout pinned at one commit, with its Node and Python
 * builders already run) and emits the tree `src/lib/hgab.ts` describes:
 *
 *   data/hgab/2027/manifest.json
 *   data/hgab/2027/overview.json                 HgabOverview
 *   data/hgab/2027/<dataset>/summary.json        HgabDatasetSummary
 *   data/hgab/2027/<dataset>/projects.parquet    PROJECT_COLUMNS, ZSTD
 *   data/hgab/2027/pdf/<doc_key>.pdf             source documents (skip with --no-pdf)
 *
 * Nothing here re-derives matching, pairing, statuses or amounts. Every row,
 * status and figure is carried from the workbench's own builders:
 *
 *   DPWH  analysis/data/comparison_projects_2027.json (+ comparison_overview,
 *         house_reading_changes, source_comparison) — buildComparisonData.mjs
 *   FMR   other-analysis/data/fmr_workbench.json     — build_fmr_workbench.py
 *   HFEP  other-analysis/data/hfep_workbench.json    — build_hfep_workbench.py
 *   NIA   analysis-nia/data/nia_workbench.json       — build_nia_workbench.py
 *   bridges are asserted equal to analysis/data/main_overview_2027.json
 *
 * Integer pesos throughout; null means "no record at this stage", never 0.
 * Stage totals are compared, never summed across stages.
 *
 *   npm run import:hgab -- --src=/tmp/dpwh-nep-review/repo --out=data/hgab/2027
 *   npm run import:hgab -- --dataset=dpwh --no-pdf
 *   npm run import:hgab -- --nep=data/2027        (our FY2027 NEP tree, for the reconciliation rows)
 */

